==Swedish==

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|sv|gml|kort}}, from {{der|sv|osx|*kurt}}, from {{der|sv|gmw-pro|*kurt}}, an early borrowing from {{der|sv|la|curtus}}.<ref name=seb/> Cognate with {{cog|de|kurz}}, {{cog|nl|kort}}, {{cog|da|kort}} and {{cog|nb|kort}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|sv|/kɔrt/}}
* {{audio|sv|Sv-kort.ogg|audio}}

====Adjective====
{{sv-adj}}

# [[short]]
#* '''1901''', {{w|Zacharias Topelius}}, [http://runeberg.org/topnovel/b0313.html ''Noveller'']
#*: Thomas! Thomas! [...]viskade nu Lotten, ty det var den '''korte''' som segrat, och hon hade igenkänt honom.
#*:: Thomas! Thomas! Lotten now whispered, since it was the short one that had won, and she had recognized him.
#* '''1931''', {{w|Hjalmar Bergman}}, [http://runeberg.org/clownjac/05.html ''Clownen Jac'']
#*: '''Kortaste''' avståndet mellan två punkter är den krokiga linjen, ju krokigare, desto '''kortare'''.
#*:: The shortest distance between two points is the crooked line, the more crooked, the shorter.

=====Declension=====
{{sv-adj-reg|n=kort}}

=====Antonyms=====
* {{l|sv|lång}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|sv|korthet}}
* {{l|sv|kortbyxor}}

===Etymology 2===
Probably from {{der|sv|da|kort||a card}} or possibly from a not referenced {{der|sv|gml|-}} word {{m|gml|kort}} known in Low German, {{m|nds|kort||a card}}.<ref name=seb>[http://runeberg.org/svetym/0434.html ''Svensk etymologisk ordbok'' ("Swedish etymological dictionary", in Swedish)]</ref> Cognate with {{cog|is|kort||a card, a map}} and {{cog|fo|kort||a card, a map}}, both from {{der|sv|non|kort||a map}}, all based on a variant of the {{der|sv|la|-}} words {{m|la|charta}} and {{m|la|carta}}.<ref name=seb/>

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|sv|/kʊrt/}}

====Noun====
{{sv-noun|n}}

# a [[card]]; a piece of stiff paper or plastic.
#* '''1926''', John Wahlborg, [http://runeberg.org/sistresa/18.html ''Sista resan'']
#*: Mannen räckte mig ett litet '''kort''', varpå han nedskrivit namn och adress på en kvinna i Stockholm.
